      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-24T23:35:27Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(tools): a form mill kind with roundover, cove, ogee, V-groove and bead presets\n\nAdd ToolKind::FormMill (file word form_mill). Its cutting edge is the\noutline in Tool::form (points [z, r, arc], a pilot length and the preset\nthat wrote them). The presets write the outline from router bit\ncatalogue numbers; the pilot band does not cut. The outline sets the\ndiameter and the flute length. An undercut outline is refused by name\n(#896). Tool::meridian and Tool::profile read the outline; the operation\nstamp hashes it.\n\nEvery operation refuses a form mill by name (it is in the CONE family\nfor the edge form work), and the 2D Chamfer names that work. The\ncatalog gets a roundover, a cove and a V-groove bit in mm and inch. The\ntool editor has the kind, a Form preset list with its number rows and\nthe pilot length; MCP add_tool and edit_tool take the form. No file\nversion step: an older build refuses the form_mill word by name.\n\nFixes #3369\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
