        "date": "2026-11-25T00:24:48Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(tools): inch form mills keep their true 3/16 in pilot; length checks take float dust\n\nThe inch roundover and cove bits state a 3/16 in pilot (4.7625 mm) and a\n11/16 in flute length (17.4625 mm) again, in place of the rounded 4.8 mm\nand 17.5 mm. The holder stack test compares the spun stack with the\ncylinder with a 1e-9 mm slack, not exact float equality. The catalogue\ntest pins the true inch pilot and flute length and the point count of\neach preset (a sharp V-groove: the tip and the top of the cone).\n\nRefs #3369\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
